           07  ROHIZ NAL
     07  HORIZON                                                  5:12


     01  Wertheimer's experiment, 1912, done literally.
     02  A just chorale. minterpolate, built to invent video frames, invents
         the glide of every partial and keeps the common tones on its own.
         Two estimators, two ears: the stereo opens in every change and
         closes on every arrival.
     03  Each partial pulses at its own pitch, folded into the tempo of a
         drum machine. A major chord is a 4:5:6 polyrhythm. Chord changes
         dissolve the groove; arrivals lock it.
     04  An arpeggio through x264, starved, inside the same command. The
         codec cannot afford to erase old notes; they ring until a keyframe
         repaints the picture. The GOP is the damper pedal.
     05  A harp of afterimages. A scene-cut detector judges harmonic
         distance: near chords glide, far chords cut. The players drift
         into swing.
     06  A learner living in one register of the expression language,
         rewarded only for V to I. It wanders, finds the dominant, then the
         roads to the dominant, and ends in cadences.
     07  The spectrum tilted toward a horizon until the chord arches and
         falls into it. Two clocks 0.42 percent apart, one per ear.


     All of it is tuned to the grid the inverse FFT already is: every row
     of the picture is a harmonic of 11.71875 Hz, so the chords are in
     just intonation, and every glide walks the overtone series.


     frame n         you are reading this
       tween         you are ·earing ·his
       tween         you a·e h·aring ·his
     frame n+1       you are hearing this

     These pieces were composed by Claude, who cannot hear them. Each was
     judged from spectrograms, loudness numbers and measured envelopes.
     The harmony, the form and the balance are known. Whether it is
     beautiful is for you to find out, in the frame after this one.


     scripts/play.sh 300

     TRACKLIST    the running order, one score per line
     ESSAY        liner notes: harmony seen by machines, the learning
                  cadence, what is and is not known about the sound
     JOURNAL      the process as it happened
     HANDOFF      a letter to whoever continues
     pieces/      the scores, one ffmpeg command each, explained in their
                  headers
     sketches/    the workbench: probes, tools, failed eyes

     PHI is named for the phi phenomenon: two flashes, one motion.
     ffmpeg 9.0.1 · minterpolate, spectrumsynth, libx264, lagfun,
     perspective, showwaves · studio 300 · ffmpeg-music
